-- title:
--   Complete linear system as a projective presentation
-- statement:
--   Let $k$ be a field, let $X$ be a scheme with at least one point, and let $f : X \to \operatorname{Spec} k$ be a morphism, which makes $\Gamma(X,\top)$ a $k$-algebra via the inverse of the canonical isomorphism $\Gamma(\operatorname{Spec} k,\top) \cong k$ followed by $f$ on global sections. Let $\mathcal N$ be a sheaf of modules on $X$ which is invertible in the sense that every point of $X$ has an open neighbourhood $U$ such that the restriction of $\mathcal N$ along $U \hookrightarrow X$ is isomorphic to the unit sheaf of rings on $U$. Assume that $\Gamma(\mathcal N,\top)$, viewed as a $k$-module by restriction of scalars along $k \to \Gamma(X,\top)$, is a finite $k$-module, and that for every $x \in X$ there are a global section $s \in \Gamma(\mathcal N,\top)$ and an open $U \ni x$ with $s$ a frame on $U$, i.e. for every open $W \le U$ the map $g \mapsto g \cdot (s|_W)$ from $\Gamma(X,W)$ to $\Gamma(\mathcal N,W)$ is bijective. Then there are $N \in \mathbb N$ and a `ProjPresentation` of $\mathcal N$ over $f$ of size $N$ — global sections $\sigma_0,\dots,\sigma_N$ of $\mathcal N$, a morphism $\pi_{\mathcal P} : X \to \operatorname{Proj}$ of the homogeneous subalgebra of $k[x_0,\dots,x_N]$ over $\operatorname{Spec} k$ recovering $f$, each $\sigma_i$ framing $\mathcal N$ on every open contained in $\pi_{\mathcal P}^{-1}D(x_i)$, and the relations $(x_j/x_i)\cdot \sigma_i|_{\pi_{\mathcal P}^{-1}D(x_i)} = \sigma_j|_{\pi_{\mathcal P}^{-1}D(x_i)}$ — whose sections form a section basis: the map $(c_i)_{i} \mapsto \sum_i f^{*}(c_i)\cdot \sigma_i$ from $k^{N+1}$ to $\Gamma(\mathcal N,\top)$ is bijective.
--
--   This is the construction of the morphism to projective space attached to the complete linear system of a line bundle generated by its global sections, packaged so that the chosen sections are simultaneously a $k$-basis of $H^0(X,\mathcal N)$ and the homogeneous coordinates of the morphism. It is used in the treatment of polarisations, for the criterion that the morphism defined by sections is a closed immersion and for the stabiliser computations for tensor powers of a line bundle; the construction of the presentation from a covering by framing opens is supplied by [`AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Modules.exists_projPresentation_of_iSup_eq_top`](thm.html#AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Modules.exists_projPresentation_of_iSup_eq_top).
